## 1. Harden the Express stack

| Issue | Why it matters | Fix |
|-------|----------------|-----|
| **Missing security headers** | Browsers won’t get protections against XSS, click‑jacking, MIME‑sniffing, etc. | Install and use **helmet**. |
| **No CORS policy** | By default any origin can call your API; you may want to restrict it. | Add **cors** with an explicit whitelist. |
| **No rate‑limiting** | Allows brute‑force or DoS attacks on `/users` or any future state‑changing routes. | Use **express-rate-limit**. |
| **Uncaught async errors** | A thrown error inside an async route will crash the process. | Centralised error‑handling middleware + `async‑handler` wrapper. |
| **No body‑parser & size limits** | Large payloads can exhaust memory; missing JSON parsing will make POST/PUT routes break. | `express.json({ limit: '1mb' })`. |
| **Hard‑coded port & secrets** | Makes it easy to accidentally ship dev credentials or change port per environment. | Use **dotenv** or config files. |

### Example “secure boot‑strap”

