## 4. Logging & monitoring  

| Why | How |
| ---- | ---- |
| **Detect anomalies, audit** | Use a structured logger (Winston, Pino) that includes request ID, IP, user‑agent, and error stack traces. |
| **Graceful shutdown** | Capture `process.on('uncaughtException')` and `process.on('unhandledRejection')`, log, then `process.exit(1)` after finishing current requests. |

```js
process.on('uncaughtException', (err) => {
  console.error('Uncaught Exception:', err);
  // Optionally flush logs, close DB connections, then exit
  process.exit(1);
});

process.on('unhandledRejection', (reason, promise) => {
  console.error('Unhandled Rejection at:', promise, 'reason:', reason);
  process.exit(1);
});
```

