## 5. Defensive coding checklist for future routes

| ✅ Checklist item | Why it matters |
|-------------------|----------------|
| Validate **all** incoming data (query, params, body, headers). | Prevent injection attacks, type‑confusion bugs. |
| Use **parameterised queries** or an ORM that auto‑escapes. | Guard against SQL/NoSQL injection. |
| Escape data before rendering in templates (if you ever use server‑side HTML). | Prevent XSS. |
| Return **generic error messages** for 5xx errors; expose details only in logs. | Avoid giving attackers internal clues. |
| Log **who** triggered the error (IP, user‑id, request‑id) without logging secrets. | Facilitates forensic analysis. |
